en:
It's been a good many years since it was last used, but at least someone still made the rounds there.
I heard they kept it up until about ten years ago, if I remember right.
Of course, nobody makes the rounds there now.{p}

Thinking they must have bolted in a hurry, he swept the light all around, but there was no sign of anyone.
Even if they had bolted, he should have caught that moment with his own eyes, and anyone moving at any real speed could not have kept the floorboards from creaking.
And yet he sensed nothing of the kind.{p}

"Where? Where are you?!"
Shouting that, Mr. Sakurai ran all over the old school building.
And no matter how fast he ran, the footsteps followed him precisely, always keeping the same distance.{p}

When she reached the third floor and shone her flashlight ahead, the corridor stretched on far longer than she'd expected.
One by one, she shone the flashlight into each classroom.
"Huh. Looks like there's nothing to it after all."{p}

She managed to get through the second floor safely too, and she was on her way down the stairs to the first floor when it happened.
She could feel air different from before sweeping right through her.
She could clearly feel her pores tightening and every hair on her body standing on end.{p}"Ugh. What is this feeling...?"{p}

Something hazy seemed to be coming toward her from the far end of the corridor.
"...?"
When she turned to look once more, this time she could see what it was.{p}

A baby on all fours, grinning from ear to ear, was heading straight for her.
Incredibly fast...
"Wh-what is that thing?!"{p}

She couldn't help quickening her pace.
For some reason, though, she couldn't run.
She felt that if she ran, things would suddenly come to a head, so she couldn't bring herself to upset this balance.{p}

Mr. Sakurai had decided to skip the patrol, but he still couldn't feel at ease about it.
I suppose it was just his nature.
"If I give up on the patrol like this..."{p}

Mr. Sakurai took a flashlight, slipped on his sandals, and headed for the old school building.
The old building standing before him now looked so huge he could hardly believe it was the same one he had patrolled earlier.
Was it because of his fear?{p}

With that in mind, Mr. Sakurai picked up the receiver once more.
"...Still no good."
Then he thought for a moment.{p}

"Who's there☆"
The instant he spun around, Mr. Sakurai aimed the flashlight where the intruder's face ought to be.
But no one was there.{p}

And the man who had been crawling down the hallway was nowhere to be seen.
"I could see him clearly, even in the dark..."
Relieved, he slumped down right where he was.{p}

The next morning he was found by the other teachers, and his whole body was covered in raised, welted scratches.
Having suffered a severe mental shock, the teacher was admitted to a hospital for treatment.
The treatment has made little progress, and they say there's no hope of recovery.{p}

"Who's there☆"
and the instant he spun around, he aimed the flashlight where its face ought to be.
But no one was there.{p}

"There's no point squaring off against the intruder here!
I have to get away for now!"
Mr. Sakurai started running.{p}

"If I turn at the end of that hall and go down the stairs, I should see the exit right away!"
He had come in sandals, so shards of glass and such had gotten in and cut his feet, but he couldn't worry about that now.
The half-ruined building was strewn with splinters of wood, making the footing terrible.{p}
